# Ill-Timed Explosion with a one-card library and nothing else in hand: the first draw gives Bot1 an Island, the second fails (CR 121.4).
# "Discard two cards" is impossible with one card in hand, and a player can't choose an impossible option (CR 608.2d), so the
# question is not asked (`! Bot1.Accept`; the control is the scenario with two cards, where it is asked). Bot1 then loses to the failed
# draw the next time state-based actions are checked.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Ill-Timed Explosion
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Island

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ill-Timed Explosion.Cast
! Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Result = Bot2 won
Bot1.Status = Lost
